/-! # Equicharacteristic complete local presentations

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tags 032A (1) and its final proof paragraph,
0326 (field-containing case), and 032C (first sentence)
(blueprint: lem-trf-equicharacteristic-complete-local-presentation).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

namespace IsLocalRing

/-- A complete Noetherian local ring containing a field has a residue-field section
and a power-series surjection taking the variables to any prescribed maximal-ideal
generators. The section need not respect the original field map.

Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, Tags 032A (1) and its final proof paragraph,
0326 (field-containing case), and 032C (first sentence)
(blueprint: lem-trf-equicharacteristic-complete-local-presentation).

Proof:
1. The composite k → C → F is injective, so k and F have the same characteristic p
and p vanishes in C. Apply lem-weil-pbc-cohen-coefficient-ring-exists to obtain a
coefficient subring Λ. Its maximal ideal is pΛ = 0, and its residue isomorphism
identifies Λ with F. Its inverse followed by Λ → C gives α with ρα = id.
2. Apply lem-trf-coefficient-field-generator-presentation with coefficient field F,
ring C, residue isomorphism the identity, section α, and the given generators y.
Its map ψ has the required constants and variable images and is surjective. Its
inverse image of the maximal ideal is the variables ideal, so ker ψ lies in that
ideal. When r = 0 the maximal ideal is zero and ψ = α is the residue inverse.
3. Apply the field case of lem-weil-pbc-power-series-field-cohen-regular-complete,
clauses (1), (3), (4), to obtain the Noetherian complete regular local source with
maximal ideal generated by the variables. This also covers r = 0, when Q = F. -/
theorem exists_equicharacteristic_complete_local_presentation
    (k : Type u) [Field k] (C : Type v) [CommRing C] [IsLocalRing C]
    [IsNoetherianRing C] [IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal C) C]
    (_ι : k →+* C) (r : ℕ) (y : Fin r → C)
    (hy : ∀ i : Fin r, y i ∈ maximalIdeal C)
    (hgen : Ideal.span (Set.range y) = maximalIdeal C) :
    (∃ (α : ResidueField C →+* C)
        (ψ : MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (ResidueField C) →+* C),
      (residue C).comp α = RingHom.id (ResidueField C) ∧
      (∀ a : ResidueField C, ψ (MvPowerSeries.C a) = α a) ∧
      (∀ i : Fin r, ψ (MvPowerSeries.X i) = y i) ∧
      Function.Surjective ψ ∧
      RingHom.ker ψ ≤ Ideal.span
        (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin r → MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (ResidueField C)))) ∧
    IsNoetherianRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (ResidueField C)) ∧
    IsAdicComplete (maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (ResidueField C)))
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (ResidueField C)) ∧
    IsRegularLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (ResidueField C)) ∧
    maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (ResidueField C)) = Ideal.span
      (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin r → MvPowerSeries (Fin r) (ResidueField C))) := by
  sorry

end IsLocalRing
